WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.750
Welcome to the Tueri Systems Risk Brief for Thursday, October twenty-ninth.

2
00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:07.564
Operational clarity when conditions change.

3
00:00:07.564 --> 00:00:12.299
A few minutes on what is happening, what can be confirmed, and what has changed.

4
00:00:12.299 --> 00:00:13.822
Digitally narrated.

5
00:00:13.822 --> 00:00:18.594
A train collision in Spain has shut the Madrid to Andalusia high-speed line.

6
00:00:18.594 --> 00:00:21.443
Houthi missiles hit the edge of Aden's airport.

7
00:00:21.443 --> 00:00:23.136
There are new shipping warnings.

8
00:00:23.136 --> 00:00:28.517
And the US Ebola attestation rule now covers aircraft crew.

9
00:00:28.517 --> 00:00:29.841
Here's the detail.

10
00:00:29.841 --> 00:00:30.709
Spain first.

11
00:00:30.709 --> 00:00:36.781
Reported: two high-speed trains collided near Urda, in Toledo province, on Wednesday morning local time.

12
00:00:36.781 --> 00:00:39.883
Media report sixty-eight dead.

13
00:00:39.883 --> 00:00:47.163
Reported, per Spain's rail infrastructure manager: the Madrid to Andalusia high-speed line is suspended with no reopening date.

14
00:00:47.163 --> 00:00:58.260
The state rail operator has stopped selling tickets on the route until December thirteenth unless the line reopens sooner, and plans a slower replacement service through Ciudad Real from Friday.

15
00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:04.682
Tueri suggests rebooking travel between Madrid and southern Spain now rather than waiting for the line.

16
00:01:04.682 --> 00:01:07.394
Yemen and Saudi Arabia.

17
00:01:07.394 --> 00:01:15.071
Reported: the Houthis called for Aden airport to be evacuated on Wednesday, then fired two ballistic missiles that struck the airport perimeter.

18
00:01:15.071 --> 00:01:21.733
Yemeni government forces report civilian injuries and damage, and transport officials say air traffic was halted.

19
00:01:21.733 --> 00:01:30.409
The US State Department issued an alert on Wednesday about Houthi attacks in Saudi Arabia, including on civilian airports.

20
00:01:30.409 --> 00:01:33.271
Still claim only: the Houthi strike on the Ras Tanura refinery.

21
00:01:33.271 --> 00:01:35.574
Saudi Arabia has not confirmed it.

22
00:01:35.574 --> 00:01:41.556
At Riyadh's main airport, Flightradar twenty-four data at about five thirty-five a.m.

23
00:01:41.556 --> 00:01:44.653
Central showed about thirteen percent of today's flights cancelled.

24
00:01:44.653 --> 00:01:49.848
Today's schedule is much smaller than yesterday's, so that is not a like-for-like improvement.

25
00:01:49.848 --> 00:01:54.288
It remains a partial reopening with observed disruption.

26
00:01:54.288 --> 00:01:56.533
Shipping.

27
00:01:56.533 --> 00:02:02.917
UK Maritime Trade Operations warned of suspicious activity in the Strait of Hormuz, off the coast of Oman, late Wednesday Central time.

28
00:02:02.917 --> 00:02:08.460
A ship's master reported seeing another vessel on fire.

29
00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:10.644
The report came from a third party, and an attack has not been confirmed.

30
00:02:10.644 --> 00:02:17.789
A separate advisory reports a suspicious small craft in the Gulf of Aden, possibly a pirate group.

31
00:02:17.789 --> 00:02:26.080
Reported, per Bulgarian authorities: three sea drones struck a container ship off Bulgaria's Black Sea coast.

32
00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:27.337
All eighteen crew were rescued, and the ship sank.

33
00:02:27.337 --> 00:02:29.862
Who launched the drones is not established.

34
00:02:29.862 --> 00:02:39.011
The latest weekly assessment from the Joint Maritime Information Center still rates the threat in the Strait of Hormuz as severe.

35
00:02:39.011 --> 00:02:41.536
Borders and health.

36
00:02:41.536 --> 00:02:53.807
New, and confirmed on the CDC's own page: an amended order issued Wednesday extends the Ebola attestation requirement to everyone on board an aircraft flying to the United States, including crew on passenger and cargo flights.

37
00:02:53.807 --> 00:02:57.833
The start is unchanged, eleven fifty-nine p.m.

38
00:02:57.833 --> 00:02:59.753
Eastern on Tuesday, November third.

39
00:02:59.753 --> 00:03:06.280
Reported, per Reuters: airline groups have urged CDC to reconsider, citing too little time to prepare.

40
00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:14.233
In Nigeria, the US Embassy's notice, now read in full, says arrivals could face quarantine or self-isolation of at least twenty-one days.

41
00:03:14.233 --> 00:03:21.342
That is a Nigerian measure relayed by the embassy; Nigeria's health authority page does not mention a quarantine period.

42
00:03:21.342 --> 00:03:27.780
Tueri suggests that crew schedulers and charter operators confirm their attestation process before Tuesday.

43
00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:29.277
Operations check.

44
00:03:29.277 --> 00:03:35.583
Hazards: reported, citing India's weather department, Arnab has weakened to a deep depression.

45
00:03:35.583 --> 00:03:39.787
State officials put the death toll at six; other tallies are higher.

46
00:03:39.787 --> 00:03:50.151
Internet: in Haiti, Cloudflare reported a complete outage on the Digicel network from Tuesday after damage to two fiber links, still down as of early Wednesday, with no restoration date given.

47
00:03:50.151 --> 00:03:58.255
Georgia Tech's measurements show Crimea and Sevastopol at about ninety-nine percent of reference levels, a recovery in the measured signal.

48
00:03:58.255 --> 00:04:03.736
Moscow's mobile internet limits were due to end today.

49
00:04:03.736 --> 00:04:04.576
Power: Sudan's grid is not confirmed fully restored.

50
00:04:04.576 --> 00:04:14.545
Labor: the US government warns of an Italian general strike from nine p.m. tonight local time to Friday evening, affecting rail and flights.

51
00:04:14.545 --> 00:04:16.529
That's today's brief.

52
00:04:16.529 --> 00:04:18.050
Current as of five forty-five a.m.

53
00:04:18.050 --> 00:04:20.875
Central, Thursday.

54
00:04:20.875 --> 00:04:21.747
Tueri summarizes public reporting.

55
00:04:21.747 --> 00:04:28.690
It is not legal, medical, or security advice for any specific situation.

56
00:04:28.690 --> 00:04:31.102
Check the original source before you act.

57
00:04:31.102 --> 00:04:40.171
Tueri Systems provides information verification, communications support, and operational decision support for organizations working in changing conditions.

58
00:04:40.171 --> 00:04:42.882
Learn more at tuerisystems.com.

59
00:04:42.882 --> 00:04:43.979
Thanks for listening.
